<article class="env-lemma" id="06EK">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/06EK">Lemma <span data-tag="06EK">67.25.6</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $X$ be an algebraic space over $S$. For any locally closed subset $T \subset |X|$ we have </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  T \not= \emptyset \Rightarrow T \cap X_{\text{ft-pts}} \not= \emptyset .  \]
</div>
  <p> In particular, for any closed subset $T \subset |X|$ we see that $T \cap X_{\text{ft-pts}}$ is dense in $T$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $i : Z \to X$ be the reduced induce subspace structure on $T$, see Remark <a href="/tag/06EC" data-tag="06EC">67.12.5</a>. Any immersion is locally of finite type, see Lemma <a href="/tag/06ED" data-tag="06ED">67.23.7</a>. Hence by Lemma <a href="/tag/06EI" data-tag="06EI">67.25.4</a> we see $Z_{\text{ft-pts}} \subset X_{\text{ft-pts}} \cap T$. Finally, any nonempty affine scheme $U$ with an étale morphism towards $Z$ has at least one closed point. Hence $Z$ has at least one finite type point by Lemma <a href="/tag/06EH" data-tag="06EH">67.25.3</a>. The lemma follows. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>